# Template development

Before making any change in this repo, read and follow `CLAUDE.md` — the
authoritative rules for the copier template that generates weisssrv tenant
repositories. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` is the map of how the template is put
together.

The rules that must hold in every change:

- Nothing here deploys; a change reaches every generated repo through
  `copier update`.
- Never hardcode site identity under `template/` — domains, registry hosts, node
  labels, VIPs and runner tags are answers, and the contrast fixture will catch
  a literal that slipped in.
- Never edit a vendored library copy; fix it upstream and re-vendor.
- `copier.yml` is API: renaming or removing a question is a breaking change.
- Run `python3 -m pytest tests` before opening a merge request.
